{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr2jc1jVWR3tyXZDKsYo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't open the repository, so this diagnosis rests on the report and my memory of the standard NestJS auth boilerplate. The line numbers are estimates. The retrieved snippets only contain e2e tests, so none of these candidates is confirmed against the actual code.\n\nThe 422 `needLoginViaProvider:google` comes from the login check that compares the stored `user.provider` with `email`. So the new user must have been saved with the wrong provider value, most likely `google`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":5024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6167d77-3e15-4271-8909-e11d53ab994a","uuid":"ffc01109-39e1-41fc-b397-cf6070595fb1","timestamp":"2026-11-08T19:41:50.693Z","request_id":"req_011Cgr2jbp5L8x2bw4zzNBLk"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr2jc1jVWR3tyXZDKsYo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HJpfdHuy3MBzKZWBGS7Y1F","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"candidates":[{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.register","start_line":125,"end_line":150,"explanation":"Email registration creates the user through usersService.create. If the call passes or defaults a provider other than AuthProvidersEnum.email, such as google, the user is stored with the wrong provider. validateLogin then rejects the login with needLoginViaProvider:google. This is the most likely place for the defect."},{"file":"src/users/users.service.ts","symbol":"UsersService.create","start_line":40,"end_line":120,"explanation":"The provider default is applied when the user is created. A wrong fallback here, or a wrong value on the entity column default, would mark email-registered users as google users."},{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.validateLogin","start_line":60,"end_line":85,"explanation":"The login check compares user.provider with AuthProvidersEnum.email and returns the 422 needLoginViaProvider error with the stored provider name. If the condition is inverted or uses the wrong enum, email users are rejected. I rank this lowest because the error message shows the stored provider is already google."}],"fix":{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","description":"In AuthService.register, create the user with provider: AuthProvidersEnum.email explicitly. In UsersService.create and the user entity column default, make email the fallback provider. Then check that validateLogin only blocks users whose provider differs from email."}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":5024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_in